{
  "name": "Making Sure Your New Lever Faucet Works Perfectly",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Installing a new lever faucet doesn't have to be a mystery. The key is following a few steps carefully to ensure everything works smoothly. First off, before you touch anything, make sure you've completely turned off the water supply at the main valves, then open the old faucet to relieve any lingering pressure. Once that's done, you can remove the old faucet. When you're ready to set the new one, pay close attention to the gasket or sealant instructions – this is crucial for preventing leaks. Gently place the new faucet through the hole, making sure it's aligned exactly how you want it, then tighten the mounting hardware evenly from underneath. Next, connect your hot and cold supply lines. Make sure these are hand-tightened first, then give them a slight turn with a wrench if needed, being careful not to overtighten. Finally, restore your water supply slowly, and then test the faucet thoroughly. Run both hot and cold water, check the spray function, and most importantly, inspect every connection point for leaks. If you run into any issues, especially with older plumbing or tricky connections, don't hesitate to reach out to HH Remodeling LLC. We're here to help homeowners in the Denver area with any installation challenges.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
